version: 2.0.0
description: Platform-specific HTTP routes for agent-driven UI, overview aggregation, git management, and ambient coordination
components:
  AgentCommandRoute:
    description: POST /api/platform/agent-command — receives navigate/highlight/annotate/observe/clear commands, broadcasts via WS
    type: route
    tags: [feature, agent-ui]
  OverviewHandler:
    description: GET /api/platform/overview — aggregates project info, symbol counts, lore stats, calibration, tasks, health metrics, and recent activity
    type: route
    tags: [feature, dashboard]
  GitRouter:
    description: /api/git/* — 8 endpoints for git status, branches, log, diff, stage, unstage, commit, push
    type: router
    tags: [feature, git]
  DocsRouter:
    description: /api/docs/* — 6 endpoints for manifest, symbol pages, flow pages, portal, custom pages, and search
    type: router
    tags: [feature, docs]
  AmbientRouter:
    description: /api/ambient/* — 5 endpoints for event stream queries, nomination management, SSE real-time streaming, and data policy
    type: router
    tags: [feature, ambient]
    signals: ["!ambient:event", "!ambient:nomination"]
  TasksRouter:
    description: /api/tasks/* — read-only HTTP over the v7 claimant task DAG (list w/ status/priority/tag/claimant filters, /board captain run-DAG, /inbox per-claimant, /calibration archetype×taskType grid, /:id). / and /board attach a computed estimate{min,max,n,source} + taskType per task (the learned-calibration story-point). Owns no storage; mutation stays on the write router.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, tasks, calibration]
  TasksWriteRouter:
    description: /api/tasks/* WRITE verbs — POST /:id/{claim,start,done,block,unblock} each PROXY the enforced updateTask state machine (no bypass), plus POST /sync (inbound two-way GitHub reconcile through the same writers). Verbs fire a best-effort outbound GitHub projection; a done settle broadcasts a live agent:annotate. portal.yaml ^write-capable.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, tasks, task-sync, enforcement]
  WarplineRouter:
    description: /api/warpline/* — READ-ONLY HTTP over the @a-company/warpline engine (the Convergence/Divergence Oracle), imported in-process (never shells the CLI). GET /ledger (reads .warpline/oracle.jsonl, version-guarded on schemaVersion, newest-first), GET /refs (local branches + HEAD), POST /forecast (ephemeral meaning forecast, no ledger write), POST /oracle (full Oracle, appends ledger), POST /diff (semantic diff), GET /absorb/:ref (serialized WarpState). An in-process concurrency semaphore (cap 2) guards every absorb-spawning handler; a per-ref WarpState cache reuses deterministic absorbs. fs.watch the ledger → !oracle-record-appended over the WS bus. NO git-write/weave path (HEAD/index/worktree untouched), but POST /oracle APPENDS to .warpline/oracle.jsonl — a state mutation declared in portal.yaml as ^write-capable while the reads + ephemeral computes are ^read-only. User refs pass an allowlist validator (REF_RE) and the engine interposes --end-of-options (git-exec) so a leading-dash ref can't be an arg-injection.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, warpline, oracle, append-only-ledger]
    signals: ["!oracle-record-appended"]
  ClassroomRouter:
    description: /api/classroom/* — READ-ONLY HTTP over the Academy (Classroom) gated-learning artifacts (TD-2026-06-19-007). GET /status (bootstrapped flag = curriculum dir has ≥1 *.syllabus; per-agent syllabi w/ status + certified/provisional counts; cert rollup w/ the HONEST repeatFailureRate = overturned/(survived+overturned), null when 0 resolved), GET /staged (the REAL staged candidates = study-hall JOURNAL entries from the ENROLLED agents only — those with a syllabus — read from each agent's GLOBAL journal ~/.paradigm/agents/<agent>/journal/*.yaml, one item per entry {agent, insight, confidence, trust, source, ts} newest-first; EXCLUDES entries already promoted to the notebook (promoted_to_notebook set) — once an entry graduates it is no longer a staged candidate (T-007); deliberately does NOT read the legacy Ambient nominations firehose — the Academy is the GATED-truth counterpart to Ambient), GET /certifications (cert rows from classroom-certifications.jsonl, each with a derived loop:'gated'|'legacy' from certifiedBy — gate→legacy, peer|quorum→gated, newest-first), GET /refinements (field-failure rows, newest-first), GET /rapsheet (per-certified-entry learning lineage joining the three loop spines — born=cert.ts ⋈ applied=notebook-refs.jsonl by entryId ⋈ broke=field-failures by entryId; each row {entryId, agent, concepts, certifiedBy, loop, outcome, bornTs, appliedCount, lastAppliedAt, breaks[]}; `breaks: []` means UNTESTED, never "passed"; sorted overturned→applied-pending→never-applied), GET /locker (Agent Locker — per-agent notebook vetting scoped to the PROJECT roster = enrolled agents ∪ agents with a project notebook, NOT the whole installed library; each agent's entries read from GLOBAL ~/.paradigm/notebooks/<agent> overlaid with PROJECT .paradigm/notebooks/<agent> deduped by id project-wins; per entry {id, title, source, trust, scope, confidence, appliedCount, brokeCount, publishable, vetted}; trust defaults to 'provisional' when unset so legacy auto-promoted entries read as BACKLOG not VETTED; vetted = trust 'certified'; sorted most-applied-first). Owns no storage; NO write endpoints. Every loader degrades to []/empty rollup on missing/malformed files (never throws on cold start). portal.yaml ^read-only.
    type: router
    tags: [feature, classroom, academy, read-only]
